# Public-repo policy: this repo (Project-VR) is public-facing. Only material a
# stranger with a G2 needs is tracked — README, the journey write-up, patches,
# scripts, infra, g2-studio, and tools code. Internal working material (research
# docs, audits, charters, run results, captures, agent instructions) stays on
# disk, out of the repo.

# Internal docs — everything under docs/ except the public journey write-up.
/docs/*
!/docs/JOURNEY.md
# Agent instruction files (machine-specific, internal).
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
# Run records / replay outputs / benchmarks (internal evidence).
/results/
# Internal findings note inside otherwise-public tools code.
/tools/led_dataset/MATCHER_FAILURE_FINDINGS.md
# Annotation datasets / batches / research notes (internal evidence, not tool code).
/tools/led_dataset/dataset/
/tools/led_dataset/batches/
/tools/led_dataset/research/
# Local safety bundles (never upload).
/.backups-*/
# Internal root-level notes.
/AUDIT.md
/RESEARCH-tearing.md
/RESEARCH-tracking.md

# Upstream source trees — separate repos with their own history, built in place.
/src/
# Regenerable NVIDIA module rollback backups.
/module-backup-*/
# Local-only / internal — never upload (kept on disk, out of the repo).
/backups/
/diagnostics/
/bench/
/recon/
/state/
/edid/
/tests/
/patches/legacy/
/patches/_index_sources/
/patches/README.md
/tools/analyze2.py
/tools/analyze_kalman.py
/tools/build-track-a.sh
/tools/install-patched-modules.sh
# Python / build cruft.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.o
# Compiled probe binary (built from vkdisplays.c).
/vkdisplays
# Stale pre-upgrade / working-state backups + research scratch (kept on disk, not tracked).
/pre-26.04-snapshot-*/
/steamvr-monado-working-backup-*/
/kalman-data/
/logs/
/captures/
.analysis-venv/
/worktrees/
vendor/
# Kernel-signing MOK (PRIVATE KEY — never commit).
/infra/mok-kernel/

# Private local evidence must never be published.
PRIVATE-HANDOFF.md
private/
private-evidence/
recordings/
config-backup/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.core
*.dmp
*.reg
*.hiv
*.pem
*.key
.env
build/
dist/

# Reviewed portable continuation documentation and synthetic tests.
!/AGENTS.md
!/docs/UPSTREAM-README.md
!/docs/PROVENANCE.md
!/docs/PUBLICATION.md
!/docs/INSTALLATION.md
!/docs/ROADMAP.md
!/docs/RELEASE-GATES.md
!/docs/DISCOVERY.md
!/docs/current/
!/docs/iterations/
!/tests/
/tests/*
!/tests/test_wmrctl.py
